# Swimming, through the real keys (owner, 2026-09-17): deep water was a wall to
# everything without a raft under it, and it is a slow crossing now for a body
# that can take it. What it costs is time and a soaking — nothing is dropped,
# nothing drowns — and most machines still stop at the waterline, which is the
# other half of the ruling and the last frame here.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/swimming.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
place spawn
wait 0.6

# --- out of its depth ------------------------------------------------------------
# `ground deep_water` stands the player where, until today, nobody could stand.
ground deep_water
wait 1.2
await swimming 4
shot 01-out-of-its-depth with swimming

# --- taking it under its own steam, on the real keys ------------------------------
walk 1,0 1.8
wait 0.4
shot 02-crossing-under-its-own-steam with swimming

# --- and out: back on the strand it went in from ----------------------------------
# Staged by name rather than walked: which way this seed's shore lies is not what
# the frame is about, and a walk that guesses it is a walk that fails elsewhere.
place spawn
wait 1.2
shot 03-ashore-and-dripping with land:coast

# --- the other half: a hunter that will not follow ---------------------------------
# The machine is put out on the only ground there is — the shore — and that is
# where it stays. Swimming away works, and the one machine it does not work on is
# the dredger, which was built for the water and says so on its own row.
#
# That the beasts come in after you (a dog swims, at a swimmer pace) and that the
# dredger crosses are proved in tests/swim/test_swim_chase.gd, in the real
# simulation: staging a chase across open water in a tour measures the runner and
# the shape of one seed bay, not the rule.
ground deep_water
wait 1.0
await swimming 4
spawn runner
wait 2.0
shot 04-it-stops-at-the-waterline with swimming,mob:runner
